{:id :EACL-FORMAL-100
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :benchmark
 :seed-or-trace "0tx scale review, 2026-10-03: lookup-resources of `open = view & subscribed` for the owner of 5 of N subscribed ledgers on Datahike; 68N - 2 fetched values, limit exceeded from N = 1,471"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release with wildcard subjects, 8.0.0-RC-2026-10-02 included"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "A lookup or count over an intersection generates its candidates from one operand, the sealed anchor, and decides the other operands per candidate. `operator-plan/select-intersection-anchor` took the operand with the smallest structural tuple [direct? sequence-compatible? depth work node-id]. A reference to a permission has depth 0 and work 1 whatever it expands to, so two named operands tied and the canonical node id, which follows the operand's name, decided; a relation always won, a wildcard relation included. An operand whose cover reads a wildcard relation holds for every subject wherever a wildcard relationship reaches, so generating from it enumerated every such resource for every subject: 68 fetched values per ledger of the platform for `view & subscribed`, and `:eacl.recursive-traversal/limit-exceeded` under the default limits from 1,471 ledgers."
 :fix
 "Sealing computes, as a least fixed point over the permission closure, the expression nodes whose candidate cover reads a wildcard branch: a relation that declares `T:*`, an arrow to one, a reference or arrow to a permission whose root is one, a union with such a child, an exclusion with such a left operand, an intersection whose operands all are. The cost entry of such a node carries `:wildcard-cover? true`, inside the plan fingerprint and only where it holds, and `select-intersection-anchor` takes such an operand only when every operand is one. Plans that read no wildcard branch are unchanged. `compiler-plan-compatibility` gains `:intersection-anchor`."
 :notes
 "The listed subject's five resources cost 5 fetched values at every platform size after the fix. An intersection whose operands all read a wildcard, and the choice among operands that read none, still follow structural costs; a choice by observed selectivity is not part of the sealed plan."
